/*!
 * @defgroup linflexd_uart LINFlexD UART Driver
 * @ingroup linflexd_driver
 * @brief UART mode driver for the LINFlexD peripheral.
 *
 * ## Key Features
 * - Configurable baud rate with fractional divider
 * - Word length: 7, 8, 15, or 16 bits
 * - Parity: even, odd, always-0, always-1; disabled only for 8/16-bit words
 * - Stop bits: 1 or 2
 * - Three transfer models: blocking, polling, and non-blocking
 * - Interrupt-driven and DMA-driven data transfer
 * - Rx/Tx callback support for continuous streaming
 * - Idle line timeout detection with configurable counter
 * - Sleep mode with automatic wakeup on bus activity
 *
 * ## Configuration
 *
 * Fill a @ref linflexd_uart_user_config_t structure and pass it to
 * LINFlexD_UART_DRV_Init(). Key fields:
 *
 * | Field             | Description                                 |
 * |-------------------|---------------------------------------------|
 * | baudRate          | Desired baud rate in bps                    |
 * | wordLength        | Data word width (7/8/15/16 bits)            |
 * | parityCheck       | Enable or disable parity                    |
 * | parityType        | Parity type when enabled                    |
 * | stopBitsCount     | Number of stop bits (1 or 2)                |
 * | txTransferType    | Interrupt or DMA for Tx                     |
 * | rxTransferType    | Interrupt or DMA for Rx                     |
 *
 * ## Usage Patterns
 *
 * ### Basic Init → Tx → Rx → Deinit
 * @code
 * linflexd_uart_state_t state;
 * linflexd_uart_user_config_t config;
 * config.baudRate       = 115200U;
 * config.wordLength     = LINFlexD_UART_8_BITS;
 * config.parityCheck    = false;
 * config.stopBitsCount  = LINFlexD_UART_ONE_STOP_BIT;
 * config.txTransferType = LINFlexD_UART_USING_INTERRUPTS;
 * config.rxTransferType = LINFlexD_UART_USING_INTERRUPTS;
 *
 * LINFlexD_UART_DRV_Init(0U, &state, &config);
 *
 * // Blocking transmit
 * LINFlexD_UART_DRV_SendDataBlocking(0U, txBuf, sizeof(txBuf), 1000U);
 *
 * // Blocking receive
 * LINFlexD_UART_DRV_ReceiveDataBlocking(0U, rxBuf, 10U, 1000U);
 *
 * LINFlexD_UART_DRV_Deinit(0U);
 * @endcode
 *
 * ## API Reference
 *
 * | Group                          | Key Functions                                     |
 * |-------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
 * | Initialization / Deinitialization | LINFlexD_UART_DRV_Init, LINFlexD_UART_DRV_Deinit |
 * | Data Transmission             | LINFlexD_UART_DRV_SendDataBlocking, LINFlexD_UART_DRV_SendData |
 * | Data Reception                | LINFlexD_UART_DRV_ReceiveDataBlocking, LINFlexD_UART_DRV_ReceiveData |
 * | Buffer Management             | LINFlexD_UART_DRV_SetTxBuffer, LINFlexD_UART_DRV_SetRxBuffer |
 * | Power Mode                    | LINFlexD_UART_DRV_GoToSleepMode, LINFlexD_UART_DRV_GotoIdleState |
 * | Timeout Configuration         | LINFlexD_UART_DRV_ConfigureTimeoutCounter         |
 *
 * ## Integration Notes
 * - The application must enable the LINFlexD peripheral clock before calling Init.
 * - Only one mode (UART or LIN) may be active per LINFlexD instance.
 * - For DMA transfers, DMA channels must be configured and the DMA driver
 *   initialized before calling Init.
 * - Callbacks execute in interrupt context; keep them short.
 *
 * @note Word lengths of 15 and 16 bits use 2-byte buffer elements.
 */